{
  "abstract": "We study sub-quadruple regular extensions of two-sided rational Diophantine quintuples in $(r, \\lambda, S_{ab})$, proving fifth elements are linear in $S_{ab}$ and cut out the Branch-1 sextuple surface $E_{Br1}$ and twin-fifth surfaces $E_{F1}, E_{F3}$. Factoring $R_4$ on regular fifths defines $S_{4,2}$, collapsing on Branch 1 to a smooth genus-three curve $H$ of relation type $(5,2)$ with unramified $d=1$ descent and a new rational almost septuple $S_7^{(20/21)}$. In global $(r,\\mu,z)$ coordinates, we construct explicit sextuple families, moving-parameter quintuples on $E_B$ (with a $2$-adic lock eliminating $Q_4\\equiv -2$), and the triple-square section $L_1=0$ of $R_5$ with rank-$2$ sublattice $\\Lambda(r)$ and rank-$0$ $E_{16}$ closure at $v=-1/5$. In $(r,u,v,\\theta)$, we prove the One-$R_5$ Lorentz Syzygy, Dual Brahmagupta reduction, blow-up $P_{blowup}=0$, and Two-Conic Master Equation $P_{surf}=0$ covering $N_{core}=0$ ($4:1$) via the Möbius decoder and Separated Binomial Law, classifying sub-regular and collision curves, the genus-$5$ slice $F_{12}=0$ (type-$(4,1)$ $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{133})$ $19/21$ septuple), Canonical Sections I ($E_{YW}$, $(19,2,10)$, $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{5})$ sextuple) and II (Dual-Reflection sextuple [4]), Rank-$4$ five-frame factorization, $r$-only reflection laws for $S_7^{(fc)}, S_7^{3refl}$, and the Three-Conic Euler system $S_6^{Euler}(r,t)$ yielding single-sided families $Q_5^{refl}(r), Q_5^{\\star}(r), S_6^{refl}(r)$ on unconstrained $(r,C_0)$. On $S_{3tors}$, we establish Master Syzygies, $1$-line selector $U_\\mp$, Five-$R_5$ root-splitting, $Q_h$ Three-Circle decomposition, $H=1/3$ $2$-descent, Branch B, and paired/antipodal source closures. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 21 integrating the complete symbolic unifications, birational dictionaries, single-sided reflection theorems, Three-Conic Euler system, and referee-audit certificates of exp50-exp63, all verified in verify_paper.py (exp9-exp63) and THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md (Items 9-22, Theorem 20(9)-(50)) in supplement.zip: (1) Two-Conic Master Equation M(beta) = 0, 4:1 Even Quotient Dictionary, Local-Global Genus Certificates, Canonical Sections of Conic 3 & Exact Rank-4 Five-Frame Pullback P_rk4(R, u^2, v^2) = 0 (exp50-exp57, exp62): Eliminated (tau, rho, F_0, F_2) on P_blowup = 0 to obtain the 259-term surface P_surf(r, alpha, beta) = 0 covering N_core(R, D_br, s_2) = 0 as a generically 4:1 (Z/2Z x Z/2Z) Galois cover factoring through the birational even quotient tilde{P}_surf(R, m, B) = 0 <-> tilde{N}_core(R, u, v) = 0 via the 1-term Mobius decoder u = -W/(gamma + ((R-1)/t_alpha)*u_b), v = -W/(gamma + t_alpha*u_b) and explicit 1-line rational inverse, Separated Binomial Law, reciprocal Atkin-Lehner master equation M_AL(beta_AL) := beta_AL^8 M(-omega/beta_AL) = 0, and Conic-3 law Q_conic = 2r(s_rho + 2r)p_rho + s_rho[(2r^2-1)s_rho + 2r(r^2-1)] = sigma_gen^2; proved via local-global discriminant-conductor completeness 2(d-1)m = sum_P(2*delta_P + e_P - 1) = deg(Delta_x) + mult_inf(Delta_x) the exact geometric genera g(F_12) = 5, g(C_slice) = 14, g(F_{6,7}) = 8, g(G_{5,5}^{(a,b)}) = 4, 5, g(C_{4,4}^{(g=a)}) = 3, and g(C_{5,5}^{(g=a)}) = 4; verified the exhaustive general F_12 divisor census across |p|, q <= 200 and the exact relation type (|R_4|, |R_5|) = (4, 1) of the all-positive Q(sqrt(133)) 19/21 almost septuple at (R, u, v) = (343/171, 47/39, -29); proved Section I (rho_2 = alpha) is birational to conductor-190 rank-1 E_{Y_W} (yielding integer N_core point (19, 2, 10) and Q(sqrt(5)) 15/15 sextuple), decomposed Section II (rho_2 = alpha + 2r) into 4 factors (bielliptic genus-2 C_{sec2,3}, C_{sec2,4} over conductor-254 rank-1 E_{4,a}, recovering at (r, alpha) = (26/11, 7/22) the Dual-Reflection 15/15 sextuple {f = c*_- = b* = a*} [4, sec 7]), and fixed the Rank-4 Five-Frame locus d_- = 2/(C_0 -+ w_1) in Theorem 20(32) using the exact One-R_5 dictionary w_1^2 = (u^2 v^2 - u^2 - v^2 + R)/(R - 1), C_0 = (d_- + d_+ - 4R(a+b))/(2(2R-1)) to prove with zero division remainder that Res_alpha(num_rk4, quad_alpha) = u^4 v^4 (R-1)^2 P_rk4(R, u^2, v^2) (64 terms, multidegree (6, 4, 2)); (2) Antipodal Quadruple Q_h, 1-Line U-Selector & Five-R_5 Root-Splitting on S_{3-tors} (exp58-exp60): Proved unconditional d_-(a,b,c) closure on Q_h (cd = -1) via rank-0 E_t : Y^2 = X(X^2 - 12X + 16) and Three-Circle decomposition; derived U_-+(r, s, kappa) for G(a, b; z_0, z_1) = 0; proved G_1 - G_2 = H(R_1 - R_2)(R_1 + R_2) on g_1 = g_2 over P_orb(v, w_z, w_e) = 0 with 3-factor h-splitting; and proved the (r, t, s) 4-factor L_1 splitting and (r, H_k) degree-halving of R_3(d, 3P_0, g); (3) Condition-20 Conic on E_{F1}, Reflection Syzygies for S_7^{(f_c)}, S_7^{3-refl}, Three-Conic System S_6^{Euler}(r, t) & Single-Sided Families Q_5^{refl}(r), Q_5^*(r), S_6^{refl}(r) on Unconstrained (r, C_0) (exp61-exp63): Parameterized Condition 20 by S_{ab}^{(-)}(r, lam, m); proved in (r, C_0, d_-) that S_7^{(f_c)} has all 5 open pairs equal to rank-1 differences of squares with r-only shifts, and on S_7^{3-refl} = {a, b, c, d_-, f_{a,-}, f_{b,-}, f_{c,-}} proved the Common-Shift Theorem 1 + x*f_{x,-} = (x + T_0)^2 - (4r_{yz}^2 - 1) (T_0 = 2(abc - rst)) and d_--independent linear reflection syzygies; introduced t = C_0/(2r(2r^2-1)) on mu_{inf}(r, C_0) (d_- = 4r^2*a) to construct S_6^{Euler}(r, t) = {a, b, c, d_-, f_{a,-}, g_{Euler,+}} (g_{Euler,+} = d_+(0, c, f_{a,-})) with 12/15 squares in Q(r, t) and 3 open pairs governed by the Universal Three-Conic System with Common Shift 4r^2 - 1; and proved that at t = t_1(r) = (4r^2-1)/(2(2r^2-1)) (C_{0,1}(r) = r(4r^2-1)), g_{Euler,+}(r, t_1) = g_{refl}(r) = d_+(a, d_-, f_{a,-}), giving single-sided type-(2,0) Q_5^{refl}(r), type-(1,0) Q_5^*(r) = {a, c, d_-, f_{a,-}, g_{refl}}, and 14/15 almost sextuples S_6^{refl}(r) subset Q(r) of relation type (3, 0).",
